Honest gaps, in priority order:
ecdsa_core for synthesis. The constant-time ladder needs a real implementation — double-and-add-always over secp256r1 with projective coordinates, scalar blinding, and base-point randomization. ~4 000 LUTs, and it is the second critical path after the SHA round.
PUF characterization. BCH parameters are chosen from an assumed 5 % BER. If the measured intra-die Hamming distance exceeds 5 %, t=128 is undersized and the design needs t=160 with a longer syndrome and a smaller key.
BCH generator polynomial. Not in the tree. Generate with a Python script over GF(2¹¹), verify deg(g) == 1408 and that g(α^i) == 0 for i = 1..256, dump to bch_g.mem. alpha_pow.mem likewise, 2 047 entries.
Fuzzy-extractor formal. Prove recon(enroll(p) with ≤t flips) == recon(enroll(p)) — a 2 047-bit datapath, needs abstraction to 64 bits.
Power analysis. The quote_signer payload assembly is fine, but the ECDSA ladder and the BCH decoder both leak. Masking budget and the TVLA setup are a separate workstream.
measure_agent.c symbol references (IE_ROOT_SEED_ADDR, _stext) are placeholder addresses needing a real linker map.

